.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-whoami - Show this node's self-identity (name, mesh ID, org, version)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel whoami [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
citadel whoami answers "am I on a Citadel node, and what is its identity?"
using local/persisted state. It requires neither sudo nor a live
\&'citadel work'/'citadel up' process -- an unregistered or offline host still
prints a well-formed report with the unavailable fields called out.

.PP
It also refreshes a stable local cache at
/identity.json (network.GetNodeConfigDir()) so an agent or
script can read a node's identity with a single file read instead of
re-deriving it every time.

.PP
Note: there is currently no numeric AceTeam fabric/platform node ID available
locally -- only the mesh (Headscale) node ID can be resolved from this host.
See aceteam #8139.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for whoami

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output in JSON format


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP
